<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kobe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kobe is a port city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-bay">Osaka Bay</a>, capital of Hyogo Prefecture. Its old harbour of Hyogo, known in the 12th century as Owada no Tomari, was developed by Taira no Kiyomori and was a chief port for trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onin-war">Onin War</a>. Opened to foreign trade in 1868, Kobe became one of Japan's largest ports and was devastated by the Great Hanshin earthquake of 1995.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kobe.jpg" alt="Kobe" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Balon Greyjoy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20190901_Kobe_harbor-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
